<title>USA: Trade estimates for USDA weekly grain export sales.</title>
<headline>Trade estimates for USDA weekly grain export sales.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade estimates for the U.S. Department of Agriculture's weekly net export sales were as follows (in tonnes). The report is slated for release at 0830 EDT on Thursday.</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Estimate Range</p>
<p>Corn (old crop)300,000 to 500,000</p>
<p>    Corn (new)     400,000 to 600,000</p>
<p>   *Wheat	    500,000 to 700,000</p>
<p>Soybeans (old)  50,000 to 150,000</p>
<p>Soybeans (new) 300,000 to 500,000</p>
<p>    Soyoil		   0 to   1,000</p>
<p>    Soymeal	   30,000 to  75,000</p>
<p>*The wheat export total includes old and new crop sales. The current (1996-97) wheat marketing year ends on May 31.</p>
<p>The export total for corn, soybeans, soyoil and soymeal are estimates for net sales for the old crop (1996-97) marketing year which ends on August 31.</p>
<p>((Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
